flowchart TB
  accTitle: CDDA interpretation stays outside shared memory and time arithmetic
  accDescr: CDDA EvidenceStore validates the current visible schema and retained bytes. A CDDA scene adapter projects literal facts, and a mission adapter authenticates exact admitted mutation payloads. Shared campaign memory consumes passive repository and source ports. The CDDA lifecycle and time adapter authenticate identity, same-turn reload continuity and canonical source endpoints before projecting seconds to pure time arithmetic. These are logical responsibilities, not independent processes or proof of another game binding. No memory or time projection grants input authority.
  V["CDDA EvidenceStore<br/>visible schema and retained bytes"] --> S["CDDA scene projection"]
  A["Mission ledger<br/>admitted payload and provenance"] --> M["Mission admission adapter<br/>CDDA identity validation"]
  S --> P["Passive repository and source ports"]
  M --> P
  V --> P
  P --> R["Shared campaign-memory reducer<br/>claims, conflicts and advisory context"]
  V --> C["CDDA lifecycle and time adapter<br/>identity and same-turn reload proof"]
  A --> C
  C -->|"Projected seconds and exact linked endpoints"| T["Shared time arithmetic<br/>within-session deltas only"]
